IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P1-annex-i`

-- P1-art6: Article 6 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): the classification rules for high-risk AI systems.
-- THE OMNIBUS inserted paragraphs 1a, 1b and 1c into Article 6 (the lines below the marker "M1 INSERTED") and changed nothing else of it. Paragraph 1 is encoded in both texts (as enacted: without 1a to 1c;
-- as amended: with them), each in its own function with no date and no gate, and a dispatcher that reads the version in force on the date asked.
-- GATES. Article 6 is in Chapter III Section 1, which applies from 2 December 2027 to AI systems classified as high-risk under Article 6(2) with Annex III and from 2 August 2028 to those classified under
-- Article 6(1) with Annex I (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c), as the Omnibus amends it; as enacted the dates were 2 August 2026 and 2 August 2027, which the Omnibus replaced before they arrived, so the as-enacted
-- text never applied: the dispatcher answers NOTHING on every date it was the text, and the ungated as-enacted function is what the tests call). Article 6(1) passes the Annex I route to the keel's gate and
-- Article 6(2) passes the Annex III route (fork F-6-gate-route); Article 6(5) is in provision group `General` (from 2 August 2026) but its deadline is 2 February 2026 (fork F-6-5-gate).
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE the text says the AI system is high-risk (or the stated consequence); JUST FALSE the text says in its own words that it is not ("shall be
-- considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled", "shall not qualify", "shall not be considered"); NOTHING not covered (the provision does not yet apply on the date asked).
-- The facts the caller states are plain: what the product is, which legislation covers it (an item of Annex I), whether a third-party conformity assessment is required; the definition of "safety component"
-- (Article 3(14)) is one BOOLEAN input here, "intended to be used as a safety component of a product"; the seat layer works it out from the facts of Article 3(14) by calling the keel's function (fork F-6-1-safety-component, seam S16).

§ `Article 6(1) and (1a), (1b), (1c): the Annex I route, as enacted`

-- "Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b)": says that independence from the product does not matter; it adds no element.
-- "shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled": a "where" condition, so a failed condition is the text's own no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:648 | 1. Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b), that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:649 | (a)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:650 | the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product, or the AI system is itself a product, covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:651 | (b)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:652 | the product whose safety component pursuant to point (a) is the AI system, or the AI system itself as a product, is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I.
@ref Art 6(1) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:648-652)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is itself a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` IS AN `Annex I item`
      `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) as enacted the AI system is high-risk` MEANS
        (`the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` OR `the AI system is itself a product`)
    AND `Annex I the legislation is listed in Annex I` `the date asked` `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled"

§ `Article 6(1), (1a), (1b), (1c): the Annex I route, as amended`

-- Paragraphs 1a and 1b say what qualifies as a safety component "for the purposes of this Regulation, including paragraph 1": an AI system solely used for non-safety aspects "shall not qualify";
-- "notwithstanding paragraph 1a" an AI system whose failure or malfunctioning would endanger health and safety "shall qualify". Paragraph 1b prevails over 1a where both are true.
-- Reading taken: 1b reaches every AI system whose failure would endanger health and safety, whether or not 1a first excluded it (fork F-6-1b-reach; the other reading: only a system 1a excluded).
-- src:223 | 1a. For the purposes of this Regulation, including paragraph 1 of this Article, AI systems that are solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control shall not qualify as safety components.
-- src:224 | 1b. Notwithstanding paragraph 1a, AI systems the failure or malfunctioning of which would endanger health and safety shall qualify as safety components.
@ref Art 6(1a) and (1b) which AI systems qualify as safety components (src:223-224)
GIVEN `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1a) and (1b) as amended the AI system qualifies as a safety component` MEANS
    IF `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety`
    THEN TRUE   -- "AI systems the failure or malfunctioning of which would endanger health and safety shall qualify as safety components"
    ELSE IF `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control`
         THEN FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not qualify as safety components"
         ELSE `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 3(14), "'safety component' means a component ... which"

-- src:225 | 1c. A product that is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety, in particular risks relating to the distribution of radio spectrum or electromagnetic interference that do not affect health and safety, shall not be considered as fulfilling the condition in paragraph 1, point (b).
@ref Art 6(1c) a conformity assessment required solely for other risks (src:225)
GIVEN `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1c) as amended the product fulfils the condition of paragraph 1, point (b)` MEANS
        `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I`
    AND (NOT `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be considered as fulfilling the condition in paragraph 1, point (b)"

-- src:219 | 1. Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b), that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:220 | (a) the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product, or the AI system is itself a product, covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:221 | (b) the product whose safety component pursuant to point (a) is the AI system, or the AI system itself as a product, is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I.
@ref Art 6(1) as amended (src:219-221)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is itself a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` IS AN `Annex I item`
      `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) as amended the AI system is high-risk` MEANS
        (   `Art 6(1a) and (1b) as amended the AI system qualifies as a safety component` `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control` `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety`
         OR `the AI system is itself a product`)
    AND `Annex I the legislation is listed in Annex I` `the date asked` `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `Art 6(1c) as amended the product fulfils the condition of paragraph 1, point (b)` `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled"

§ `Article 6(1): the dispatcher on the date asked, gated by Chapter III`

-- The gate is the keel's (Article 113 with Article 111(2)'s saving) for the Annex I route. FALSE from the gate means "does not apply on the date asked", which is NOTHING here, never JUST FALSE (fork F-111-2-nothing).
-- Counted for split site (iii): this function can answer NOTHING because of the gate and Article 111(2), since it passes the placement date to the keel.
-- Seam S14 (fork F-S14-reach): Article 6(1) is among the provisions that Article 2(2) leaves applying to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products, so this function does not call the keel's `Art 2(2) ...`; neither does any other function of P1 (Article 5, Article 6(2) to (8), Article 7 and the Annexes are not provisions of such a system).
-- src:219 | 1. Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b), that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:220 | (a) the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product, or the AI system is itself a product, covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:221 | (b) the product whose safety component pursuant to point (a) is the AI system, or the AI system itself as a product, is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I.
-- src:222 | ▼M1 INSERTED
-- src:223 | 1a. For the purposes of this Regulation, including paragraph 1 of this Article, AI systems that are solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control shall not qualify as safety components.
-- src:224 | 1b. Notwithstanding paragraph 1a, AI systems the failure or malfunctioning of which would endanger health and safety shall qualify as safety components.
-- src:225 | 1c. A product that is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety, in particular risks relating to the distribution of radio spectrum or electromagnetic interference that do not affect health and safety, shall not be considered as fulfilling the condition in paragraph 1, point (b).
@ref Art 6(1) with paragraphs 1a, 1b, 1c (src:219-225)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is itself a product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` IS AN `Annex I item`
      `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the AI system is high-risk` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to AI systems classified under Article 6(1) with Annex I from 2 August 2028 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(ii)), and Article 111(2) can save a system placed on the market earlier
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                       -- VERSION as enacted
            JUST (`Art 6(1) as enacted the AI system is high-risk` `the date asked` `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` `the AI system is itself a product` `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I`)
        WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                       -- VERSION as amended
            JUST (`Art 6(1) as amended the AI system is high-risk` `the date asked` `the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product` `the AI system is solely used for non-safety related aspects of user assistance, performance optimisation, service efficiency, automation or convenience or quality control` `the failure or malfunctioning of the AI system would endanger health and safety` `the AI system is itself a product` `the Union harmonisation legislation that covers the product` `the product is within the part of the legislation that the Annex lists` `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` `the product is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment solely due to risks other than risks to health and safety`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled" (a failed condition gives JUST FALSE inside the helpers above)

§ `Article 6(2) and (3): the Annex III route, the derogation, profiling`

-- Paragraph 2: "AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk." The class "AI systems referred to in Annex III" is handed to the list: a system no point lists is not referred to
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F-6-2-list). Paragraph 3: "By derogation from paragraph 2, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall not be considered to be high-risk where it does not pose a significant risk of harm ...,
-- including by not materially influencing the outcome of decision making", and the second subparagraph: "The first subparagraph shall apply where any of the following conditions is fulfilled": (a) to (d).
-- Reading taken: the derogation needs BOTH the absence of a significant risk (first subparagraph) AND at least one of (a) to (d) (second subparagraph) (fork F-6-3-cumulative; the other reading: the absence of a significant risk alone,
-- the conditions being examples). "Notwithstanding the first subparagraph, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall always be considered to be high-risk where the AI system performs profiling of natural persons":
-- profiling defeats the derogation.
-- src:227 | 2. In addition to the high-risk AI systems referred to in paragraph 1, AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk.
-- src:228 | 3. By derogation from paragraph 2, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall not be considered to be high-risk where it does not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons, including by not materially influencing the outcome of decision making.
-- src:229 | The first subparagraph shall apply where any of the following conditions is fulfilled:
-- src:230 | (a) the AI system is intended to perform a narrow procedural task;
-- src:231 | (b) the AI system is intended to improve the result of a previously completed human activity;
-- src:232 | (c) the AI system is intended to detect decision-making patterns or deviations from prior decision-making patterns and is not meant to replace or influence the previously completed human assessment, without proper human review; or
-- src:233 | (d) the AI system is intended to perform a preparatory task to an assessment relevant for the purposes of the use cases listed in Annex III.
-- src:234 | Notwithstanding the first subparagraph, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall always be considered to be high-risk where the AI system performs profiling of natural persons.
@ref Art 6(2) and (3) (src:227-234)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system performs profiling of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system does not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons, including by not materially influencing the outcome of decision making` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is intended to perform a narrow procedural task` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is intended to improve the result of a previously completed human activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is intended to detect decision-making patterns or deviations from prior decision-making patterns and is not meant to replace or influence the previously completed human assessment, without proper human review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is intended to perform a preparatory task to an assessment relevant for the purposes of the use cases listed in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) the AI system is high-risk` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to AI systems classified under Article 6(2) with Annex III from 2 December 2027 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(i)), and Article 111(2) can save a system placed on the market earlier
        IF NOT `the AI system is referred to in Annex III`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk" (the class is handed to the list of Annex III)
        IF `the AI system performs profiling of natural persons`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "an AI system referred to in Annex III shall always be considered to be high-risk where the AI system performs profiling of natural persons"
        IF     `the AI system does not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons, including by not materially influencing the outcome of decision making`
           AND (   `the AI system is intended to perform a narrow procedural task`
                OR `the AI system is intended to improve the result of a previously completed human activity`
                OR `the AI system is intended to detect decision-making patterns or deviations from prior decision-making patterns and is not meant to replace or influence the previously completed human assessment, without proper human review`
                OR `the AI system is intended to perform a preparatory task to an assessment relevant for the purposes of the use cases listed in Annex III`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an AI system referred to in Annex III shall not be considered to be high-risk where it does not pose a significant risk of harm" (the derogation of paragraph 3)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- "AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk"

§ `Article 6: the route by which the AI system is high-risk (seam S1)`

-- The two paragraphs add up: "In addition to the high-risk AI systems referred to in paragraph 1, AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk." A system high-risk under both takes the Annex III route,
-- which applies from the earlier date (fork F-6-both-routes); the other parts take the route as the input `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`.
-- NOTHING when neither paragraph answers (the Chapter III date has not arrived for either route on the date asked).
-- src:219 | 1. Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b), that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:
-- src:227 | 2. In addition to the high-risk AI systems referred to in paragraph 1, AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk.
@ref Art 6(1) and 6(2) together (src:219) (src:227)
GIVEN `whether Article 6(1) makes the AI system high-risk` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `whether Article 6(2) makes the AI system high-risk` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Route to high-risk`
`Art 6 the route by which the AI system is high-risk` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `whether Article 6(2) makes the AI system high-risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
        IF `whether Article 6(1) makes the AI system high-risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I`
        IF `whether Article 6(1) makes the AI system high-risk` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `whether Article 6(2) makes the AI system high-risk` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST `Route neither`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled" and "AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III has not begun to apply on the date asked, under either route

§ `Article 6(4): the provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk`

DECLARE `Art 6(4) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(4) document the assessment`
    `Art 6(4) provide the documentation of the assessment`

-- "shall document its assessment before that system is placed on the market or put into service": the clock starts on the day the provider considers the AI system not high-risk and runs to the day before
-- the placing on the market or putting into service ("before" excludes the day itself; fork F-6-4-before). A negative time limit (the consideration came on or after the placing) is a breach at once.
-- src:235 | 4. A provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk shall document its assessment before that system is placed on the market or put into service. Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2). Upon request of national competent authorities, the provider shall provide the documentation of the assessment.
@ref Art 6(4) first sentence: document the assessment before the placing (src:235)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the provider considers that the AI system is not high-risk` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 6(4) duty`
`Art 6(4) the duty to document the assessment before the AI system is placed on the market or put into service` MEANS
    IF     `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
       AND `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk`
    THEN
        PARTY Provider
        MUST `Art 6(4) document the assessment`
        WITHIN ((Day `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`) MINUS 1) MINUS (Day `the date on which the provider considers that the AI system is not high-risk`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the assessment was not documented before the AI system was placed on the market or put into service"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2)": JUST TRUE for the provider who considers its Annex III system not high-risk; NOTHING otherwise (the sentence is about "such provider").
-- src:235 | 4. A provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk shall document its assessment before that system is placed on the market or put into service. Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2). Upon request of national competent authorities, the provider shall provide the documentation of the assessment.
@ref Art 6(4) second sentence: the registration obligation (src:235)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(4) the provider is subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from 2 December 2027 on the Annex III route (Article 113 third paragraph, point (c)(i))
        IF `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "a provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk"

-- "Upon request of national competent authorities, the provider shall provide the documentation of the assessment": a duty gated by "upon request"; no time limit and no stated consequence: no breach path.
-- src:235 | 4. A provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk shall document its assessment before that system is placed on the market or put into service. Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2). Upon request of national competent authorities, the provider shall provide the documentation of the assessment.
@ref Art 6(4) third sentence: provide the documentation upon request (src:235)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `national competent authorities have requested the documentation of the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 6(4) duty`
`Art 6(4) the duty to provide the documentation of the assessment upon request` MEANS
    IF     `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
       AND `the provider considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk`
       AND `national competent authorities have requested the documentation of the assessment`
    THEN
        PARTY Provider
        MUST `Art 6(4) provide the documentation of the assessment`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the documentation of the assessment was not provided upon request of national competent authorities"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

