§ `Article 6(5): the Commission's guidelines`

DECLARE `Art 6(5) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 6(5) provide the guidelines`

-- "The Commission shall, after consulting the Board, and no later than 2 February 2026, provide guidelines": the party is the Commission (an official; no seat). The deadline is fixed in the text.
-- Article 113 puts Article 6(5) in the provision group `General`, which applies from 2 August 2026, six months AFTER the deadline (fork F-6-5-gate, finding in NOTES.md). The clock is armed when the Regulation
-- enters into force (1 August 2024) and runs to 2 February 2026, as the keel does for Article 111; on a date before the Regulation is in force nothing is owed.
-- src:236 | 5. The Commission shall, after consulting the European Artificial Intelligence Board (the ‘Board’), and no later than 2 February 2026, provide guidelines specifying the practical implementation of this Article in line with Article 96 together with a comprehensive list of practical examples of use cases of AI systems that are high-risk and not high-risk.
@ref Art 6(5) the guidelines no later than 2 February 2026 (src:236)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 6(5) duty`
`Art 6(5) the duty of the Commission to provide guidelines` MEANS
    IF `Art 113 the Regulation is in force` `the date asked`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 6(5) provide the guidelines`
        WITHIN (Day (Date 2 2 2026)) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the Commission did not provide the guidelines no later than 2 February 2026"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- Whether Article 6(5) applies on the date asked, by Article 113's own provision group `General` (from 2 August 2026): the date the keel gives is later than the deadline.
-- src:236 | 5. The Commission shall, after consulting the European Artificial Intelligence Board (the ‘Board’), and no later than 2 February 2026, provide guidelines specifying the practical implementation of this Article in line with Article 96 together with a comprehensive list of practical examples of use cases of AI systems that are high-risk and not high-risk.
@ref Art 6(5) is in provision group General (src:236)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(5) the provision applies on the date asked under Article 113` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Article 6(6), (7) and (8): delegated acts amending paragraph 3, second subparagraph`

-- These three paragraphs are in Chapter III Section 1: Article 113 third paragraph, point (c) excepts only Article 6(5), so they apply from 2 December 2027 on the Annex III route (the paragraphs amend
-- paragraph 3, which is about Annex III systems). As in P1-art7, the gate is passed the date asked as the placement date: the Commission's power is not about one AI system (fork F-7-gate).

-- Paragraph 6: "The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend paragraph 3, second subparagraph, ... by adding new conditions ... or by modifying them, where there is concrete and
-- reliable evidence ...". A power gated by "where": the periods ruling's rule (b) gives JUST FALSE where the evidence is absent (split site (ii), fork F-6-6-where; the other reading is NOTHING). Official; no seat question.
-- src:237 | 6. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend paragraph 3, second subparagraph, of this Article by adding new conditions to those laid down therein, or by modifying them, where there is concrete and reliable evidence of the existence of AI systems that fall under the scope of Annex III, but do not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons.
@ref Art 6(6) the power to add or modify conditions (src:237)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `there is concrete and reliable evidence of the existence of AI systems that fall under the scope of Annex III, but do not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
