        OTHERWISE JUST `there is concrete and reliable evidence of the existence of AI systems that fall under the scope of Annex III, but do not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons`
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is concrete and reliable evidence" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a failed "where")

-- Paragraph 7: "The Commission shall adopt delegated acts ... by deleting any of the conditions laid down therein, where there is concrete and reliable evidence that this is necessary to maintain the level of protection".
-- A duty gated by "where": JUST FALSE where the gate fails (the guide keeps JUST FALSE for a duty). No time limit and no stated consequence: no breach path.
